# CODEOWNERS - ownership-based review routing.
#
# Philosophy: normal PRs (dependency bumps, docs, code) merge without a
# mandatory human approval. Files on the TRUST BOUNDARY - CI pipelines,
# dependency policy, release automation, security governance - require
# explicit approval from a listed owner. Enforcement lives in the
# "trust-boundary-codeowner-review" repository ruleset (active on the
# default branch, "require review from code owners").
#
# Replace @Oloompa with your maintainer identity/team when bootstrapping
# a new project from this template (see MANIFEST.md).

# Default: no global owner. Add one here if you want every file reviewed.
# *       @your-org/maintainers

# --- Trust boundary (human approval required) -----------------------------

# The whole automation and governance surface under .github/: CI/CD
# workflows, PR classification (trust-boundary.yml), dependency policy,
# review-routing rules (this file), and PR/issue templates.
/.github/                      @Oloompa

# Hook configuration (quality gate guardrail). NOTE: /Makefile is
# deliberately NOT owned - AI agents may extend build targets freely.
/.pre-commit-config.yaml       @Oloompa

# Release automation
/release-please-config.json    @Oloompa
/.release-please-manifest.json @Oloompa

# Governance and legal
/LICENSE                       @Oloompa
/SECURITY.md                   @Oloompa

# Security scanning policy
/.gitleaks.toml                @Oloompa
/.gitleaksignore               @Oloompa

# Ruleset provisioning script (grants the protections above)
/scripts/                      @Oloompa
